{"id":1006,"date":"2020-11-17T15:15:06","date_gmt":"2020-11-17T23:15:06","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1006"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:41","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:41","slug":"how-to-use-the-arduino-ide","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/how-to-use-the-arduino-ide\/","title":{"rendered":"How to Use the Arduino IDE"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ee4890f\" name=\"6a2215ee4890f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Briefing video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video will show you the basics of the Arduino IDE. You still need to look at the rest of the lesson though![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=V_nt3Gdd5gQ&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ee48a38\" name=\"6a2215ee48a38\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Create a sketch<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you want to create a new file, you&#8217;ll need to click on the third button, which looks like a sheet of paper. This will create a sketch, which is what you&#8217;ll be writing our code on. It&#8217;s your programming workspace![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1009&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ee48a8b\" name=\"6a2215ee48a8b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Void setup and void loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In every new sketch, make sure you include void setup() and void loop(). They&#8217;re the prompts that start your programs, and without them, you won&#8217;t be able to run any code on the Arduino IDE.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1011&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ee48af2\" name=\"6a2215ee48af2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The different buttons<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In addition to the create new sketch button, you will also have your:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Compile button, which is the check mark icon. It checks that your code is compiled, or set up correctly.<\/li>\n<li>Upload button, which is the icon with the arrow pointing to the right. It lets you upload your code to your Smart Inventor Board.<\/li>\n<li>Open button, which is the up arrow with a line underneath. This opens the last sketch that you saved.<\/li>\n<li>Save button, which is the down arrow with a line underneath. This saves the sketch that you are working on.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1012&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1013&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1014&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1015&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ee48b39\" name=\"6a2215ee48b39\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Serial monitor<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The serial monitor button is on the righthand side, and it looks like a magnifying glass. The serial monitor displays the number, or values, that your sensors are reading, and it&#8217;s really useful if you don&#8217;t have another visual display![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1017&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ee48bcf\" name=\"6a2215ee48bcf\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Libraries<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>You&#8217;ll probably be using libraries in most of your Rokit Smart programs. Libraries are sets of reusable functions and resources, and can help you with your own code once you use them. If you need to find the libraries that you&#8217;re working with, go to\u00a0Sketch &gt; Library in Arduino. In our example, we&#8217;re using the Servo library.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__step-media\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1020&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215ee48c49\" name=\"6a2215ee48c49\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The tools tab<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You will use the tools tab every time you need to check that you have the right board and port. Make sure you&#8217;re always connected to the\u00a0&#8220;Rokit-Smartinventor-mega32&#8243; board with your version and your chosen port![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1021&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Briefing video [vc_column_text]This video will show you the basics of the Arduino IDE. You still need to look at the rest of the lesson though![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=V_nt3Gdd5gQ\" align=\"center\"]&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/how-to-use-the-arduino-ide\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1732,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,626,1533,1438,144,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2184,2183,2122,2171],"class_list":["post-1006","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-arduino-ide","lesson-tag-building","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-programming","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1006","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1006\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1022,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1006\/revisions\/1022"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1732"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1006"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1006"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1006"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/